{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T04:47:06.286437", "query": "postpartum depression mein kya karna chahiye", "reply": "To address postpartum depression, it's essential to take a holistic approach. Going out daily, even if it's just for a short walk to a park or a playground, can be beneficial. However, it's also crucial to consider professional help. Consulting a therapist or a counselor who specializes in postpartum depression can provide valuable guidance and support. Additionally, ensuring adequate rest, maintaining a healthy diet, and staying connected with family and friends can also help manage symptoms. If you're experiencing severe symptoms, it's vital to reach out to a healthcare professional for proper evaluation and treatment.", "mode": "data", "score": 0.637, "response_time_ms": 767.57}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T04:47:10.081457", "query": "baby bottle accept nahi kar raha kya karein", "reply": "Bottle accept nahi kar raha hai, toh aapko thoda patience rakhna hoga. Aap baby ko bottle se paani ya formula milk dena shuru karein, lekin thoda-thoda karke. Agar baby refuse karta hai, toh aap usko breast feed kar sakte hain. Aap bottle ko alag-alag position mein try kar sakte hain, jaise ki upright ya side mein. Agar phir bhi baby bottle accept nahi karta, toh aap doctor se consult kar sakte hain.", "mode": "data", "score": 0.684, "response_time_ms": 849.53}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T04:47:15.492748", "query": "when should I introduce cow milk", "reply": "It's recommended to avoid introducing cow's milk to your baby until they are at least 1 year old.", "mode": "data", "score": 0.769, "response_time_ms": 2393.58}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T04:47:23.150161", "query": "what supplements should breastfeeding mother take after c section", "reply": "After a C-section, breastfeeding mothers should consider taking supplements to support their health and milk production. The recommended supplements include Vitamin B complex, Vitamin C, iron, and calcium. These supplements can help support the mother's overall health and ensure the baby is receiving adequate nutrients through breast milk. It's generally advised to take these supplements for 1-3 months postpartum. Additionally, Vitamin D3 is also recommended. It's essential to consult with a healthcare provider before starting any supplements to determine the best course of action for individual needs.", "mode": "data", "score": 0.868, "response_time_ms": 2763.19}
