{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T06:49:51.390699", "query": "how long breast milk can be stored", "reply": "Breast milk can be stored at room temperature for up to 6-8 hours, but it's recommended to use it within 4-6 hours for optimal quality. However, if you're looking for a more specific guideline, here are some general storage guidelines: \n- Room temperature (up to 73°F/23°C): 4-6 hours\n- Insulated cooler with ice packs: 24 hours\n- Refrigerator (up to 39°F/4°C): 3-5 days\n- Freezer (0°F/-18°C or below): 6-12 months \n\nIt's essential to label and date the stored breast milk and use the oldest ones first. Always check the milk for any signs of spoilage before feeding it to your baby.", "mode": "data", "score": 0.919, "response_time_ms": 975.99}
