{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T06:58:29.251000", "query": "infant is not passing stool for 3 days", "reply": "For a 3-day delay in passing stool, it's essential to ensure the infant is well-hydrated. You can try giving the infant plenty of water and a fiber-rich diet if they are on solid foods. If the infant is exclusively breastfed, continue breastfeeding as usual. If the infant is formula-fed, ensure the formula is being prepared correctly, and consider adding a small amount of water to the feed. \n\nCan you please tell me the infant's age and whether they are showing any signs of distress or pain?", "mode": "data", "score": 0.768, "response_time_ms": 2937.64}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T06:58:36.712545", "query": "chhote bachche ko solid food kab se shuru karein", "reply": "Aapka sawal hai ki chhote bachche ko solid food kab se shuru karein. Jab aapka bachcha 6 mahine ka ho jata hai, to aap usko solid food de sakte hain. Lekin yeh zaruri hai ki aap pehle usko ek ek cheez dekar dekhein, jaise ki sabse pehle rice cereal, phir fruits, phir vegetables, aur phir proteins. Isse aapko pata chalega ki kya usko koi allergy hai ya nahi. Aur sabse zaruri baat, aapko apne doctor se consult karna chahiye, woh aapko best advice de sakte hain.", "mode": "data", "score": 0.652, "response_time_ms": 3195.41}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T06:58:44.660412", "query": "baby ke nappy area mein lali aa gayi hai", "reply": "It seems like your baby has developed a redness in the nappy area, which could be a sign of a diaper rash. To help soothe and prevent further irritation, you can try applying a thin layer of petroleum jelly or a diaper rash cream to the affected area after each diaper change. Also, make sure to change the diaper frequently and keep the area clean and dry. If the redness persists or worsens, it's best to consult a pediatrician for further guidance. Can you tell me if your baby is experiencing any other symptoms, such as discomfort or fever?", "mode": "data", "score": 0.774, "response_time_ms": 2774.67}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T06:58:51.712713", "query": "my baby is teething and very irritable what helps", "reply": "During teething, it's common for babies to be irritable. To help soothe your baby, you can try giving them a teething toy or a cold teether to chew on. You can also gently massage their gums with your finger. Sometimes, a pacifier or a comfort object can provide relief. If your baby is over 6 months old, you can try offering a small amount of cool water or a chilled teething ring. Additionally, maintaining a routine and ensuring your baby gets enough rest can help reduce irritability. If your baby is still distressed, you may want to consider consulting with your pediatrician for further guidance. What is your baby's age, and have you tried any of these methods already?", "mode": "data", "score": 0.724, "response_time_ms": 1909.95}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T06:58:59.781128", "query": "mujhe depression ho raha hai delivery ke baad kya karoon", "reply": "Aapko delivery ke baad depression ho raha hai, yeh ek common problem hai. Aapko apne doctor se milna chahiye, ve aapko proper guidance denge. Aap apne pati ya parivaar ke saath bhi baat kar sakti hain, unka support aapke liye bahut zaroori hai. Aapko exercise bhi karna chahiye, jaise ki yoga ya walk, yeh aapke mood ko theek karne mein madad karega. Aur haan, aapko apne baby ke saath quality time bitana chahiye, yeh aapke bond ko mazboot banayega. Agar aapko lagta hai ki aapki depression bahut badh rahi hai, to aapko counseling ya therapy leni chahiye.", "mode": "data", "score": 0.801, "response_time_ms": 1974.39}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T06:59:07.645910", "query": "my baby has runny nose and sneezing a lot", "reply": "For a runny nose and sneezing, you can try using nasal saline to help loosen and clear out the mucus. This is a gentle and safe approach for babies. If the symptoms persist or worsen, it would be helpful to know more details such as your baby's age and any other symptoms they might be experiencing.", "mode": "data", "score": 0.814, "response_time_ms": 1683.21}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T06:59:15.589581", "query": "gaye ka doodh bachche ko kab se de sakte hain", "reply": "Aapke sawal ka jawab hai ki gaye ka doodh bachche ko 1 saal ke baad de sakte hain, lekin yeh zaruri hai ki aap isse dhyan se introduce karein. Pehle thoda sa doodh mix karke dekar dekhein ki koi allergy to nahi ho rahi hai. Agar sab theek rahe to phir aap isse regular diet mein shaamil kar sakte hain.", "mode": "data", "score": 0.779, "response_time_ms": 2875.83}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T06:59:22.751888", "query": "after cesarean what vitamins should I take while nursing", "reply": "While nursing after a cesarean, it's essential to continue taking supplements that support your health and your baby's development. I recommend taking iron, calcium, and vitamin D3 supplements. \n\nFor iron, the typical dose is 30-60 mg per day, but I would need to know your weight to provide a more accurate recommendation. \n\nFor calcium, a common dose is 500-700 mg per day, but again, your weight and other factors can influence the ideal dosage.\n\nVitamin D3 is crucial for bone health, and a typical dose is 600-800 IU per day. However, to provide a more specific recommendation, I would need to know your current vitamin D levels and weight.\n\nIt's also important to note that you should consult with your healthcare provider before starting any supplements, especially after a cesarean. They can help you determine the best course of action and recommend the most suitable supplements for your individual needs.\n\nCan you please tell me your weight so I can provide more tailored advice?", "mode": "data", "score": 0.672, "response_time_ms": 2071.26}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T06:59:30.621265", "query": "infant skin is very flaky and rough what to apply", "reply": "To address your infant's flaky and rough skin, I recommend applying a thick layer of Vaseline or any emollient before sleep. Additionally, ensure your baby is well-hydrated by giving them plenty of water. You can also try applying coconut oil or Sudocream to help moisturize and soothe the skin. If the issue persists, we may need to explore other options. Can you tell me more about your baby's current skin care routine and if you've noticed any other symptoms?", "mode": "data", "score": 0.695, "response_time_ms": 1814.84}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T06:59:38.830734", "query": "bacha feeder se doodh nahi pita kya karein", "reply": "Bacha feeder se doodh nahi pita to aap kuch tareeke try kar sakte hain. Pehla, feeder ka nozzle thoda soft ho toh use change karke dekhein. Dosra, feeder ko thoda warm karke dekhein, shayad bacha warm milk pasand karta ho. Teesra, feeder ko ek angle par hold karein, jisse bacha easily doodh pe sake. Aur, agar bacha abhi bhi doodh nahi pita, toh aap breastfeeding ya bottle feeding try kar sakte hain. Kya aapne pehle se koi tareeka try kiya hai?", "mode": "data", "score": 0.707, "response_time_ms": 3189.94}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T06:59:46.039035", "query": "can I give ragi to my 6 month old baby", "reply": "At 6 months, babies can start having solid foods, and ragi is a good option. You can introduce ragi to your baby in the form of a porridge or malt. Start with a small amount, about 1-2 teaspoons, and gradually increase the quantity as your baby gets accustomed to it. Make sure to cook the ragi well and mix it with breast milk or formula to achieve a suitable consistency. Also, ensure that the ragi is free from any added sugars or salts. Would you like to know more about the preparation method or any specific precautions to take while introducing ragi to your baby?", "mode": "data", "score": 0.918, "response_time_ms": 1960.9}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T06:59:54.024426", "query": "how much water should I give to a 7 month old baby", "reply": "For a 7-month-old baby, you can give 50-100 ml of water per day, in addition to breast milk or formula. It's also a good idea to offer a few sips of water after solids to help with digestion and to get the baby used to drinking water. However, please note that breast milk or formula should still be the primary source of hydration. Would you like to know more about introducing water to your baby's diet or have any other concerns?", "mode": "data", "score": 0.943, "response_time_ms": 2803.42}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T07:00:00.964914", "query": "kya breastfeeding ke dauran dental treatment safe hai", "reply": "Breastfeeding ke dauran dental treatment generally safe hai, lekin aapko apne dentist ko batana hoga ki aap breastfeeding kar rahe hain. Kuch dental procedures, jaise ki X-rays, local anesthesia, ya antibiotics, breastfeeding par impact dal sakte hain. Aapke dentist aapko specific guidance denge.", "mode": "data", "score": 0.715, "response_time_ms": 2748.7}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T07:00:07.796507", "query": "how to burp a baby who falls asleep while breastfeeding", "reply": "If the baby falls asleep while breastfeeding, you can try to burp them gently without waking them up. However, if the baby is already asleep, you can place them on an inclined plane for 15-20 minutes after feeding, and then lay them down straight. This can help prevent any discomfort or gas buildup. Alternatively, you can also try to burp the baby before they fall asleep, by sitting them up or holding them upright for a few minutes after feeding. If you're concerned about the baby's feeding or sleeping patterns, I'd be happy to help you further. Can you tell me a bit more about your baby's feeding schedule and sleep patterns?", "mode": "data", "score": 0.802, "response_time_ms": 2817.96}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T07:00:15.623463", "query": "vitamin d drops kab tak dene chahiye", "reply": "For a baby, vitamin D drops are usually recommended until they are at least 2 years old, but this can vary depending on several factors such as the baby's diet, sun exposure, and overall health. It's best to consult with your pediatrician for a personalized recommendation. \n\nIn general, if your baby is receiving enough sunlight and has a balanced diet that includes vitamin D-fortified foods, you may be able to stop the vitamin D drops sooner. However, it's always best to follow the advice of your pediatrician. \n\nCan you please tell me your baby's current age and any other relevant details so I can provide more specific guidance?", "mode": "data", "score": 0.783, "response_time_ms": 2843.26}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T07:00:22.592332", "query": "can I give banana to my 7 month old", "reply": "You can give banana to your 7-month-old baby. It's a good source of nutrients, especially potassium. Make sure to mash it well and remove any strings or lumps to reduce the risk of choking. You can start with a small amount, about 1-2 teaspoons, and gradually increase the amount as your baby gets accustomed to it. Also, ensure the banana is ripe and soft to make it easier for your baby to digest.", "mode": "data", "score": 0.765, "response_time_ms": 1730.04}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T07:00:29.934317", "query": "baby ko colic hai kya karein", "reply": "Baby ko colic hai to aap kuch cheezein try kar sakte hain. Pehli baat, aap apne baby ko upright position mein rakhein, jisse unhein aram mile. Dusri baat, aap apne baby ko gale lagakar chhote-chhote strokes se massage karein, jisse unhein relaxation mile. Teesri baat, aap apne baby ko warm water se bath karayein, jisse unhein aram mile. Agar phir bhi baby ko colic hai to aap doctor se consult karein, woh aapko better advice de sakte hain. Kya aapne apne baby ko kabse colic hai aur unki age kya hai?", "mode": "data", "score": 0.836, "response_time_ms": 2188.55}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T07:00:37.817228", "query": "normal weight gain for exclusively breastfed baby", "reply": "For an exclusively breastfed baby, a normal weight gain is typically around 150-200 grams per week during the first 3-4 months. After 4-6 months, the weight gain usually slows down to around 100 grams per week. \n\nTo assess if your baby's weight gain is normal, I would need to know your baby's current age, weight, and birth weight. Could you please provide me with this information?", "mode": "data", "score": 0.753, "response_time_ms": 2719.79}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-28T07:00:44.646053", "query": "how to introduce eggs to 6 month old baby", "reply": "To introduce eggs to a 6-month-old baby, start by making a puree. Hard-boil an egg, then finely grind it in a mixie or blender. Begin with a small amount, about a teaspoon, and mix it with breast milk or formula to create a familiar taste and texture. Gradually increase the amount as your baby becomes accustomed to it. Always check for any signs of allergy or intolerance, such as rash, itching, or digestive issues, after introducing eggs.", "mode": "data", "score": 0.692, "response_time_ms": 1595.72}
